 "display": {
  "title": "Rabbi Akiva's Great Rule: Love Your Fellow as Yourself",
  "title_basis": "content",
  "summary_short": "Rabbi Akiva calls 'love your fellow as yourself' a great rule of the Torah, and the Alter Rebbe teaches that Ahavas Yisroel leads to loving Hashem.",
  "summary_long": "A short talk from the Tzivos Hashem radio show. Uncle Yossi quotes the verse 'Love your fellow as yourself' and Rabbi Akiva's famous saying that it is not just one more rule but a great rule of the whole Torah: when we truly love one another, we come to love Hashem and keep all the other mitzvos. He adds the Alter Rebbe's teaching that Ahavas Yisroel leads to Ahavas Hashem, and explains it with a simple example. If you really love a friend, you show it by being kind to the friends he loves too. Hashem loves every single Jew, so the way to show our love for Hashem is to love everyone He loves.",
  "lesson": "To show that you love Hashem, love every Jew, because Hashem loves each one of them.",
